{"result":"{
  "metadata": {
    "id": "292749334",
    "title": "TSD: Inventory — SFCC ↔ MuleSoft ↔ NewStore / AP21",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/292749334",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Adobe SFCC"
    },
    "version": 4,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "1. Overview\n-----------\n\nInventory in the Zimmermann SFCC platform is owned by **NewStore** (OMS) and managed upstream by **AP21** (ERP). MuleSoft acts as the integration layer in both directions:\n\n* **Inbound (AP21 → NewStore):** Stock levels are pushed from AP21 into NewStore on a scheduled basis (DC and store stock)\n* **Outbound (NewStore → SFCC):** Inventory availability is exported from NewStore and imported into SFCC via a scheduled sync\n\nSFCC does **not** connect to AP21 or NewStore directly — all inventory data passes through MuleSoft.\n\n---\n\n2. End-to-End Data Flow\n-----------------------\n\nDefaultnoneAP21 (ERP)\n│\n├──► stock-prc-api (DC stock) ──► NewStore ─────────────────────►┐\n└──► stock-prc-api (Store stock) ──► NewStore │\n│\nNewStore ──► inventory-sync-prc-api ──► [export ZIP via S3] ──► SFCC│\n│ │\n(transform to SFCC format) │\n▼ ▼\nSFCC Inventory Import Job\n(per-site inventory lists)\n\n---\n\n3. Inbound: AP21 → MuleSoft → NewStore\n--------------------------------------\n\n### 3.1 DC Stock Upload\n\n| Attribute | Detail |\n| --- | --- |\n| API | `stock-prc-api` + `newstore-sys-api` |\n| Trigger | Daily scheduler at 2:00 AM EST + on-demand REST endpoint |\n| Scope | Distribution centre (DC) locations — delta + full |\n| JIRA | ZMOBLD-263 |\n\n**Flow:** 1. Scheduler triggers (or REST call with `fromDate` + `countryCode`) 2. MuleSoft validates DC IDs, stock quantities, and product info 3. Creates import job in NewStore (`POST /api/import`) 4. Starts the job (`POST /api/import/{id}/start`) 5. Polls job status (`GET /api/import/{id}`) until complete\n\n### 3.2 Store Stock Upload\n\n| Attribute | Detail |\n| --- | --- |\n| API | `stock-prc-api` + `newstore-sys-api` |\n| Trigger | One-time full load (initial migration) + scheduler |\n| Scope | All physical boutique locations |\n| JIRA | ZMOBLD-248 |\n\n**Flow:** 1. MuleSoft validates store IDs, quantities, and product info 2. Pushes full stock dataset to NewStore (`POST /api/stock_import`)\n\n---\n\n4. Outbound: NewStore → MuleSoft → SFCC\n---------------------------------------\n\n### 4.1 Inventory Sync Process\n\n| Attribute | Detail |\n| --- | --- |\n| API | `inventory-sync-prc-api` |\n| Trigger | Scheduled every 15 minutes |\n| Regions | GB (UK), AU, US |\n| JIRA | ZMOBLD-262, ZAUBLD-233 |\n\n**Flow (per region):**\n\nDefaultnoneScheduler (every 15 min)\n│\n├─ 1. Read region codes from config (GB / AU / US)\n├─ 2. GET all stores from NewStore\n├─ 3. Filter active stores for region (exclude configured concession stores for AU/US)\n├─ 4. GET all locations (stores + DCs) from NewStore\n├─ 5. Filter enabled DCs from inclusion list in config\n├─ 6. Build group name: {REGION}\\_GROUP\\_{SHA256(store\\_ids + dc\\_ids)}\n│ Example: AU\\_GROUP\\_01EA7311C557C99DB4CD44C8208AB01...\n├─ 7. Create/verify fulfillment location group in NewStore\n│ (store group name in Anypoint Object Store)\n├─ 8. GET availability\\_export\\_id for group\n├─ 9. GET S3 URL for compressed inventory file\n├─ 10. Download + decompress ZIP from S3\n├─ 11. Transform: extract product\\_id + qty (ATP), map store\\_view by region:\n│ GB → uk\\_store\\_view, AU → default, US → us\\_store\\_view\n└─ 12. POST transformed payload to SFCC inventory import endpoint\n\n### 4.2 SFCC Inventory Configuration\n\nEach site has a dedicated inventory list referenced in `preferences.xml` (`SiteInventoryList`). All inventory list XML files live under `data/core/inventory-lists/` and are imported via the core data bundle.\n\nZimmermannUS and ZimmermannUSIntl share the same inventory list (`inventory_m_us`) — both sites fulfil from the same US stock pool.\n\n| Site | Inventory List | Sync Region |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ZimmermannAU | `inventory_m_au` | AU |\n| ZimmermannUK | `inventory_m_uk` | GB |\n| ZimmermannUS | `inventory_m_us` | US |\n| ZimmermannUSIntl | `inventory_m_us` | US (shared pool with ZimmermannUS) |\n| ZimmermannEU | `inventory_m_eu` | [To be confirmed] |\n| ZimmermannEUIntl | `inventory_m_eu_intl` | [To be confirmed] |\n| ZimmermannHK | `inventory_m_hk` | [To be confirmed] |\n| ZimmermannME | `inventory_m_me` | [To be confirmed] |\n\n> **Note:** The current MuleSoft `inventory-sync-prc-api` syncs GB, AU, and US regions. Sync coverage for EU, EUIntl, HK, and ME is to be confirmed with the integration team.\n\n---\n\n5. SFCC Cartridge Touchpoints\n-----------------------------\n\n| Touchpoint | Detail |\n| --- | --- |\n| Inventory list per site | Set in `SiteInventoryList` preference in `preferences.xml` |\n| Availability display | OOTB SFCC product availability checking against the per-site inventory list |\n| Real-time stock for boutiques | Separate MuleSoft call via Find In Store API — see [Find In Store TSD](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/292487173) |\n| Inventory import | Triggered by scheduled MuleSoft job; no cartridge code required |\n\n---\n\n6. Error Handling & Monitoring\n------------------------------\n\n| Scenario | Handling |\n| --- | --- |\n| Group already exists in NewStore | 409 response — compare stored group name; create new group if hash differs |\n| Export job status: failed / partially\\_failed | Log error; do not update Object Store last-sync date |\n| Export job status: processing / waiting | Re-poll status |\n| HTTP failures (any API call) | Retry up to 3 times, 1-minute interval |\n| Payload failure | Automated email alert with error context |\n\n---\n\n7. Key Design Decisions\n-----------------------\n\n| Decision | Choice | Rationale |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Inventory ownership | NewStore | OMS is the source of truth for fulfilment availability |\n| Group naming | SHA256 hash of store + DC IDs | Deterministic across retries and scheduled runs; no collision risk |\n| Sync frequency | Every 15 minutes | Balance between freshness and API rate limits |\n| SFCC inventory model | Per-site inventory list (not shared, except US/USIntl) | Each site has different fulfilment locations and stock pools |\n| US / USIntl shared inventory | Both sites use `inventory_m_us` | US domestic and US international orders fulfil from the same US stock pool |\n\n---\n\n8. Open Items\n-------------\n\n| # | Item | Owner |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Confirm SFCC inventory import endpoint URL and auth method | Integration Lead |\n| 2 | Define concession store exclusion list for AU and US regions | Zimmermann Ops |\n| 3 | Confirm MuleSoft inventory sync region coverage for EU, EUIntl, HK, ME sites | Integration Lead / Platform team |",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "page_width": "fixed-width"
  }
}"}

